<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49442" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">turbellae</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">turbēlae</span></b> , ārum, f.
		dim.
		turba. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A bustle</i>, <i>stir</i>, <i>row</i> (only in vulg. lang.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tantas turbellas facio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Bacch. 4, 9, 134</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">id. Ps. 1, 1, 108</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">App. de Deo Socr. p. 48,
			20</span></i>.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A little crowd</i>, <i>multitude</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">populi circumfluentis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 4, p. 151, 39 al.</span></i>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
